er choke-800 m-b-spacer-lg"><span data-content="2-143629">Hackney Council are committed to doing everything within our power to deliver net zero emissions across council functions by 2040,&nbsp;ten years earlier than the target set by the government.&nbsp;The council has control over about 5% of the borough’s emissions, which is why they are seeking to&nbsp;work together with everyone in their community to create a greener, healthier Hackney<span>. This will help cut energy use, tackle pollution and boost biodiversity.</span></span></p></div><div class="flex flex-center"><figure class="brand-figure w-100"><img src="https://cdn4.sharein.com/abundance/cms/390e0d67-38ae-4989-8400-4c67e643c85f.jpg" width="800" height="450" alt="Title placeholder text" loading="lazy"> <figcaption data-content="2-143632">Investors money has funded real green energy projects in Hackney</figcaption></figure></div></div></div></div></section></div>
